==============================================================================
(1) HARD<->EASY correspondence: SPEED-COUNT bookkeeping + the genuine 13-speed family
==============================================================================
  *** BOOKKEEPING CORRECTION (load-bearing): LRC(14) is about |S|=13 speeds.
      The naive 'hard family' {1..13} u {14m} has |S|=14 -> that is the N=15 case,
      NOT ours.  Indeed M({1..14})=1/15<1/14, but that is the tight 14-speed AP for
      LRC(15), irrelevant to LRC(14).  A GENUINE 13-speed covering set must DROP one
      of {1..13} to make room for the parked w.  So the hard 13-cores are the
      SINGLE-DROP cores {1..13}\{e} (plus possibly further drops), NOT the full AP.
      DEMO: {1..14} has |S|=14, M=1/15=0.066667 < 1/14 (N=15 tight AP, NOT a LRC(14) counterexample).

  Genuine 13-speed hard family: C_e = {1..13}\{e}, parked w=14m.  M(C_e u {w}):
    drop e= 6, w= 14: |S|=13 cov=True prim=True M=      2/23=0.086957  (>1/14? True)
    drop e= 6, w= 28: |S|=13 cov=True prim=True M=      2/23=0.086957  (>1/14? True)
    drop e= 6, w= 84: |S|=13 cov=True prim=True M=      2/23=0.086957  (>1/14? True)
    drop e=12, w= 14: |S|=13 cov=False prim=True M=      1/12=0.083333  (>1/14? True)
    drop e=12, w= 28: |S|=13 cov=False prim=True M=      1/12=0.083333  (>1/14? True)
    drop e=12, w= 84: |S|=13 cov=True prim=True M=      7/89=0.078652  (>1/14? True)
    drop e=11, w= 14: |S|=13 cov=False prim=True M=      1/11=0.090909  (>1/14? True)
    drop e=11, w= 28: |S|=13 cov=False prim=True M=      1/11=0.090909  (>1/14? True)
    drop e=11, w= 84: |S|=13 cov=False prim=True M=      1/11=0.090909  (>1/14? True)
    drop e= 1, w= 14: |S|=13 cov=True prim=True M=       1/8=0.125000  (>1/14? True)
    drop e= 1, w= 28: |S|=13 cov=True prim=True M=      2/15=0.133333  (>1/14? True)
    drop e= 1, w= 84: |S|=13 cov=True prim=True M=      2/15=0.133333  (>1/14? True)
  PEEL RULE (well-defined): given a covering 13-set S, peel the SMALLEST w with 14|w;
  C=S\{w} is a 12-speed core.  If C imprimitive, dilate by 1/gcd (scale-invariance,
  THM-522).  meas(G_C) >= meas(G_S) always (deleting a runner enlarges the safe set).

