(2) KEY LOWER BOUND: can ANY w (14|w) cover the extremal cores' G_C?  EXHAUSTIVE
==============================================================================

  CORE DROP6 {1..5,7..13} (extremal, meas=7/858): meas(G_C)@gap-1/14=7/858=0.00815851  r=4 arcs  widest=0.002706
    decoupling floor (6/7)meas - r/(7w) > 0  <=>  w > r/(6 meas) = 81.71  -> for w >= 83 (mult of 14) floor>0 => L>0 guaranteed.
    NO w (14|w, w<=2000) makes C u {w} tight.  min positive L over these w: 1543/294294=0.00524306 at w=98.
    => for EVERY w with 14|w, M(C u {w}) >= 1/14 (transversality holds for this core).

  CORE GW-easy {1..11,13} (drop e=12): meas(G_C)@gap-1/14=426/35035=0.01215927  r=4 arcs  widest=0.004082
